1
00:00:00,040 --> 00:00:02,240
This series was created
for entertainment purposes.

2
00:00:02,240 --> 00:00:05,680
The characters, actions, locations,
dialogue, languages, ceremonies,

3
00:00:05,680 --> 00:00:08,120
and artistic elements depicted in this series

4
00:00:08,120 --> 00:00:10,040
are fictional and based on imagination,

5
00:00:10,040 --> 00:00:13,920
incorporating the beauty
of the region's diverse cultures,

6
00:00:13,920 --> 00:00:18,400
including those
of Lanna, Myanmar, the Tai peoples, and China.

7
00:00:18,400 --> 00:00:20,560
It is not intended to disrespect any history,

8
00:00:20,560 --> 00:00:23,600
ethnic group, organization, profession,
or group of individuals.

9
00:00:23,600 --> 00:00:26,040
Viewer discretion is advised.

10
00:00:26,040 --> 00:00:27,200
[Previously]
<i>Fongnuan.</i>

11
00:00:27,200 --> 00:00:29,000
<i>Who is... Fongnuan?</i>

12
00:00:29,000 --> 00:00:30,120
<i>Where is this place?</i>

13
00:00:30,120 --> 00:00:31,200
<i>Ullavee.</i>

14
00:00:31,200 --> 00:00:33,440
<i>Now that you've returned,
I see how much you've grown.</i>

15
00:00:33,440 --> 00:00:36,960
<i>Thank you for your great support
for the Crown Prince.</i>

16
00:00:36,960 --> 00:00:38,200
<i>You've just returned from the battlefield.</i>

17
00:00:38,200 --> 00:00:41,400
<i>Have you bathed in the sacred spring yet?</i>

18
00:00:41,400 --> 00:00:46,120
<i>Will bathing in the sacred spring
make me a beloved son?</i>

19
00:00:48,000 --> 00:00:49,640
<i>Who are you?</i>

20
00:00:53,960 --> 00:00:56,000
<i>I'll pretend I never saw you here.</i>

21
00:00:56,920 --> 00:00:59,200
<i>You still have a life to live,</i>

22
00:01:00,200 --> 00:01:02,400
<i>so live it happily.</i>

23
00:01:03,840 --> 00:01:05,960
"You still have a life to live,"

24
00:01:08,720 --> 00:01:11,080
"so live it happily."

25
00:01:13,040 --> 00:01:14,520
That's true.

26
00:01:16,960 --> 00:01:19,600
At least you're still alive, Na Boon.

27
00:01:21,040 --> 00:01:22,840
As for Fongnuan...

28
00:01:22,840 --> 00:01:26,360
Let's see what you've got.

29
00:01:33,120 --> 00:01:35,280
Pretty nice face.

30
00:01:35,280 --> 00:01:37,480
Clear skin, too.

31
00:01:37,480 --> 00:01:39,480
Much clearer than mine.

32
00:01:39,480 --> 00:01:42,000
Your hair is long too.

33
00:01:43,080 --> 00:01:45,160
It looks healthy.

34
00:01:45,160 --> 00:01:47,600
Long and thick too.

35
00:01:53,960 --> 00:01:56,320
Being you isn't so bad.

36
00:01:57,320 --> 00:01:58,760
Fongnuan.

37
00:02:00,200 --> 00:02:02,440
From now on,

38
00:02:03,680 --> 00:02:05,440
let's collab.

39
00:03:59,680 --> 00:04:04,520
[If You Can't Die,
You Might As Well Be Happy]

40
00:04:15,800 --> 00:04:19,760
Lady Fongnuan, are you sure you want
to go to the market looking like that?

41
00:04:24,520 --> 00:04:26,880
- Isn't it pretty?
<i>- Not pretty.</i>

42
00:04:26,880 --> 00:04:28,960
You look like a madwoman.

43
00:04:28,960 --> 00:04:30,600
What do you mean?

44
00:04:30,600 --> 00:04:33,640
What woman in her right mind
ties her hair like that?

45
00:04:33,640 --> 00:04:35,160
Only madwomen do.

46
00:04:35,160 --> 00:04:38,720
It's my hair. I can do whatever I want with it.

47
00:04:38,720 --> 00:04:40,840
This is called a braid.

48
00:04:42,080 --> 00:04:43,760
It's so pretty.

49
00:04:43,760 --> 00:04:45,440
- It's not.
- It is!

50
00:04:45,440 --> 00:04:46,680
- It's not!
- It is!

51
00:04:46,680 --> 00:04:47,840
- It's not.
- It is!

52
00:04:47,840 --> 00:04:49,320
- It's not.
- It is!

53
00:04:49,320 --> 00:04:50,640
It's not!

54
00:04:51,480 --> 00:04:53,440
You're the mad one!

55
00:04:53,440 --> 00:04:54,640
No, you are!

56
00:04:54,640 --> 00:04:58,280
You're calling someone else mad out of nowhere.
You're the mad one.

57
00:04:58,280 --> 00:05:00,640
- You're the mad one.
- You blind fool!

58
00:05:00,640 --> 00:05:02,080
You mad, blind fool!

59
00:05:02,080 --> 00:05:05,800
Whatever are you talking about?
Have you gone mad?

60
00:05:05,800 --> 00:05:08,160
- You're the mad one!
- Lady Fongnuan.

61
00:05:09,600 --> 00:05:11,320
He's a prince.

62
00:05:11,320 --> 00:05:14,880
You can't behave
or speak to a prince like that.

63
00:05:19,120 --> 00:05:20,440
Sorry.

64
00:05:27,520 --> 00:05:29,840
Please accept my apologies, Your Highness.

65
00:05:29,840 --> 00:05:31,000
Ever since that day,

66
00:05:31,000 --> 00:05:34,760
Lady Fongnuan has yet to fully regain her wits.

67
00:05:39,400 --> 00:05:41,120
Lady Fongnuan.

68
00:05:41,120 --> 00:05:43,280
Mad and insolent.

69
00:07:29,680 --> 00:07:31,600
Red hibiscus.

70
00:07:32,920 --> 00:07:35,800
The real Courtesan House.

71
00:07:35,800 --> 00:07:38,360
I've only ever read about it in books.

72
00:07:39,800 --> 00:07:41,360
So this is what it's like in real life.

73
00:07:41,360 --> 00:07:43,680
That's called the Mhai flower.

74
00:07:44,560 --> 00:07:45,880
Lady Fongnuan,

75
00:07:45,880 --> 00:07:50,640
I don't think we should be hanging around
outside the Courtesan House.

76
00:07:50,640 --> 00:07:53,400
The villagers will wag their tongues.

77
00:07:57,360 --> 00:07:58,920
Lady Fongnuan!

78
00:08:23,960 --> 00:08:25,200
Your Highness!

79
00:08:26,640 --> 00:08:29,800
Madwoman! Don't call me "Your Highness."

80
00:08:29,800 --> 00:08:32,000
And you mustn't tell anyone you saw me here!

81
00:08:34,240 --> 00:08:36,240
Why do you talk like Prince...

82
00:08:36,240 --> 00:08:39,400
I said you mustn't speak like that!

83
00:08:43,400 --> 00:08:46,880
- Why do you have to call me a madwoman?
- Look at your hair.

84
00:08:46,880 --> 00:08:49,600
Look at you. You look like a madwoman.

85
00:08:49,600 --> 00:08:51,520
One moment you're here,
the next you're somewhere else.

86
00:08:51,520 --> 00:08:55,400
If Saen Thep hadn't claimed
you were Princess Maneethip's sister,

87
00:08:55,400 --> 00:08:58,320
you'd have been arrested and punished
the day we met.

88
00:08:59,720 --> 00:09:01,360
Lady Fongnuan.

89
00:09:02,600 --> 00:09:05,480
Lady Fongnuan? Lady Fongnuan!

90
00:09:10,920 --> 00:09:12,360
Lady Fongnuan...

91
00:09:13,240 --> 00:09:14,560
who were you speaking with?

92
00:09:14,560 --> 00:09:17,440
- A madman.
- A madman?

93
00:09:17,440 --> 00:09:21,600
Didn't I tell you not to come in here?
You shouldn't be talking to a madman.

94
00:09:21,600 --> 00:09:25,280
- Why can't I?
- It's unbecoming of a lady.

95
00:09:27,040 --> 00:09:30,760
I told you not to come in here.
Let us go before someone sees us.

96
00:09:30,760 --> 00:09:31,880
We must hurry.

97
00:09:31,880 --> 00:09:35,120
Lha, we haven't even seen the inside.
Must we leave now?

98
00:09:35,120 --> 00:09:37,440
- We must leave now!
- We'll take our leave, then!

99
00:09:51,720 --> 00:09:54,160
That madwoman seems trustworthy enough.

100
00:10:06,720 --> 00:10:07,960
Lha...

101
00:10:09,400 --> 00:10:14,040
how lucky you are
to be in Ullavee at this time.

102
00:10:18,160 --> 00:10:20,040
The weather is nice.

103
00:10:21,840 --> 00:10:24,160
There's no PM 2.5 pollution.

104
00:10:32,800 --> 00:10:35,080
Do you believe in reincarnation?

105
00:10:36,480 --> 00:10:37,960
As in,

106
00:10:38,680 --> 00:10:41,560
people dying and being reborn.

107
00:10:41,560 --> 00:10:44,400
Living many lifetimes, that sort of thing.

108
00:10:45,000 --> 00:10:47,080
Indeed, I do.

109
00:10:47,080 --> 00:10:49,800
We have 32 souls.

110
00:10:49,800 --> 00:10:52,400
In a sense, we all have 32 lives.

111
00:10:52,400 --> 00:10:54,000
So...

112
00:10:54,760 --> 00:10:56,760
the two of us...

113
00:10:57,960 --> 00:11:00,920
I guess our souls have been intertwined
across many lifetimes.

114
00:11:02,640 --> 00:11:05,000
That's why we've met again in this life.

115
00:11:06,840 --> 00:11:09,160
<i>How long have you been betraying me?</i>

116
00:11:09,960 --> 00:11:11,520
<i>Tell me!</i>

117
00:11:12,840 --> 00:11:15,320
<i>Boon, I... I...</i>

118
00:11:15,320 --> 00:11:17,600
<i>I'm sorry.</i>

119
00:11:17,600 --> 00:11:19,760
<i>I didn't mean to.</i>

120
00:11:20,320 --> 00:11:23,800
<i>- Boon, hear me out. I wasn't going to--
- Save it!</i>

121
00:11:23,800 --> 00:11:26,320
<i>You're just one guy. I don't care.</i>

122
00:11:28,560 --> 00:11:32,520
<i>- Hey, I'm sorry.
- How could you do this to me?</i>

123
00:11:32,520 --> 00:11:36,240
<i>I really didn't mean to, Boon. I'm sorry.</i>

124
00:11:36,240 --> 00:11:39,640
<i>How long have we been friends, Eva?</i>

125
00:11:40,800 --> 00:11:43,920
<i>We can usually talk about anything, can't we?</i>

126
00:11:45,920 --> 00:11:48,000
<i>If you like him,</i>

127
00:11:49,400 --> 00:11:51,120
<i>you could've just told me.</i>

128
00:11:52,560 --> 00:11:54,760
<i>Boon, I'm really sorry.</i>

129
00:11:54,760 --> 00:11:57,200
<i>You're so heartless.</i>

130
00:12:00,440 --> 00:12:02,280
It's fine.

131
00:12:02,280 --> 00:12:06,760
I'll just forget what happened.

132
00:12:07,560 --> 00:12:10,040
Let's start over, Eva.

133
00:12:12,920 --> 00:12:14,160
I mean, Lha.

134
00:12:17,120 --> 00:12:18,920
Yes.

135
00:12:18,920 --> 00:12:20,840
Let us start over, my lady.

136
00:12:22,600 --> 00:12:24,040
Okay.

137
00:12:24,040 --> 00:12:25,880
Deal.

138
00:12:25,880 --> 00:12:27,920
Right now, I'm Fongnuan.

139
00:12:27,920 --> 00:12:30,560
Eva, you're Lha.

140
00:12:31,760 --> 00:12:33,080
Yes.

141
00:12:34,120 --> 00:12:36,800
Are you quite well, Lady Fongnuan?

142
00:12:36,800 --> 00:12:38,520
Do you have a headache?

143
00:12:40,840 --> 00:12:43,240
I'm getting worried.

144
00:12:46,840 --> 00:12:48,800
I'm okay.

145
00:12:51,080 --> 00:12:53,320
I'm getting hungry.

146
00:12:53,320 --> 00:12:55,440
Let's go home.

147
00:12:55,440 --> 00:12:58,440
Ever since I woke up, I've been so stressed.

148
00:12:58,440 --> 00:13:01,200
I haven't had a proper meal.

149
00:13:01,200 --> 00:13:02,880
By the way,

150
00:13:02,880 --> 00:13:04,680
what's good to eat around here?

151
00:13:06,000 --> 00:13:08,560
- Well...
- Never mind.

152
00:13:08,560 --> 00:13:11,160
- Let's go and find something to eat.
- Yes.

153
00:13:11,160 --> 00:13:13,440
Lady Fongnuan, please wait for me.

154
00:13:33,800 --> 00:13:36,280
These look delicious.

155
00:13:36,280 --> 00:13:40,120
So... let me dig in!

156
00:13:40,840 --> 00:13:42,520
Wash your hands first.

157
00:13:54,360 --> 00:13:56,400
It's bad luck to take rice
from the middle of the basket.

158
00:13:56,400 --> 00:13:59,680
We won't harvest enough rice
to feed ourselves this year.

159
00:13:59,680 --> 00:14:01,360
Do you not remember?

160
00:14:02,400 --> 00:14:06,800
Then where should I take it from
to make sure we have enough?

161
00:14:06,800 --> 00:14:08,800
Take it from the edge of the basket.

162
00:14:12,280 --> 00:14:14,400
Then shape it into a bite-sized ball.

163
00:14:16,960 --> 00:14:18,120
Wait.

164
00:14:18,120 --> 00:14:22,080
It's bad luck to bite into rice like that.
You must shape it into a bite-sized ball.

165
00:14:23,320 --> 00:14:25,440
Bad luck again?

166
00:14:27,240 --> 00:14:30,160
No taking rice from the middle of the basket.

167
00:14:30,160 --> 00:14:32,040
No biting the rice.

168
00:14:32,040 --> 00:14:34,400
I'll remember that.

169
00:14:35,000 --> 00:14:38,280
Can I... eat now?

170
00:14:43,280 --> 00:14:45,360
Princess Maneethip,

171
00:14:45,360 --> 00:14:49,760
I don't think she's quite herself yet.

172
00:14:51,720 --> 00:14:54,360
Shall I summon a revered master

173
00:14:54,360 --> 00:14:56,880
to perform a Soul Recalling Ceremony
for her, my lady?

174
00:14:56,880 --> 00:14:58,360
So delicious.

175
00:14:59,040 --> 00:15:01,480
You're an amazing cook.

176
00:15:02,280 --> 00:15:04,760
Sister Maneethip, you're amazing.

177
00:15:05,680 --> 00:15:07,560
Whatever are you talking about?

178
00:15:07,560 --> 00:15:09,720
Do not try to charm me.

179
00:15:09,720 --> 00:15:13,400
If you like it, then eat your fill.
And eat properly.

180
00:15:14,680 --> 00:15:16,000
All right.

181
00:15:25,440 --> 00:15:27,840
Sister, eat.

182
00:15:27,840 --> 00:15:29,160
You go ahead.

183
00:15:29,160 --> 00:15:31,360
Do not blame me if I eat it all.

184
00:15:32,960 --> 00:15:34,120
Lha.

185
00:15:35,200 --> 00:15:36,960
I cannot, my lady.

186
00:15:38,080 --> 00:15:41,080
So... this is all for me?

187
00:15:52,240 --> 00:15:54,720
So much has happened in just one day.

188
00:15:56,000 --> 00:16:00,120
It'd be nice to at least see my mom
while I'm here.

189
00:16:00,120 --> 00:16:02,520
I even saw Eva.

190
00:16:04,520 --> 00:16:07,240
Who knows what the future will bring?

191
00:16:08,840 --> 00:16:11,640
Whatever will be, will be, I guess.

192
00:16:18,320 --> 00:16:20,320
What language did you just speak?

193
00:16:25,040 --> 00:16:27,520
English, Your Highness.

194
00:16:27,520 --> 00:16:29,080
English?

195
00:16:30,000 --> 00:16:32,520
It's spoken by foreigners,

196
00:16:32,520 --> 00:16:37,240
the tall, fair-skinned,

197
00:16:37,240 --> 00:16:39,520
and golden-haired people.

198
00:16:39,520 --> 00:16:41,000
Westerners.

199
00:16:42,000 --> 00:16:43,640
I know them.

200
00:16:43,640 --> 00:16:45,920
I've heard merchants talk about them
at the market.

201
00:16:46,840 --> 00:16:49,120
But how did you know their language?

202
00:16:52,400 --> 00:16:55,560
Ever since I awoke during the ceremony,

203
00:16:55,560 --> 00:16:58,320
I've somehow been able to speak it.

204
00:16:59,280 --> 00:17:01,880
I was probably punished
by the guardian spirits.

205
00:17:04,160 --> 00:17:05,640
How strange.

206
00:17:06,240 --> 00:17:07,960
But that's good.

207
00:17:07,960 --> 00:17:09,880
Will you teach me sometime?

208
00:17:10,680 --> 00:17:12,240
Of course.

209
00:17:13,560 --> 00:17:17,920
Shall we... exchange favors?

210
00:17:19,800 --> 00:17:21,520
There are so many princes here.

211
00:17:21,520 --> 00:17:22,920
I still can't remember them all.

212
00:17:22,920 --> 00:17:26,720
I don't want to mistake anyone for someone else
and get myself punished.

213
00:17:27,360 --> 00:17:31,520
Could you tell me who they are?

214
00:17:31,520 --> 00:17:33,960
I don't want to get into trouble again.

215
00:17:33,960 --> 00:17:36,720
<i>Ullavee is a tributary kingdom.</i>

216
00:17:36,720 --> 00:17:40,600
<i>It's situated between three powerful empires.</i>

217
00:17:40,600 --> 00:17:41,960
[Ullavee: The Forbidden Kingdom]

218
00:17:41,960 --> 00:17:45,240
The king's first son,

219
00:17:45,240 --> 00:17:50,800
our eldest brother is Prince Indraraja.

220
00:17:51,440 --> 00:17:55,800
He's the Crown Prince,
or the heir to the throne.

221
00:17:56,400 --> 00:18:01,320
<i>The first prince is the king's favorite.</i>

222
00:18:01,320 --> 00:18:02,320
[6 Princes]

223
00:18:02,320 --> 00:18:04,080
<i>The favorite child.</i>

224
00:18:05,600 --> 00:18:10,240
What about you, Prince Saen Thep?
What's your title?

225
00:18:10,240 --> 00:18:11,440
I'm the Third-in-Line.

226
00:18:11,440 --> 00:18:14,200
<i>The second is wise
in the management of state affairs.</i>

227
00:18:14,200 --> 00:18:16,280
[2nd Prince: Manages State Affairs]

228
00:18:16,280 --> 00:18:19,720
The next one is Prince Kong Tai.

229
00:18:19,720 --> 00:18:21,880
<i>Not pretty. You look like a madwoman.</i>

230
00:18:21,880 --> 00:18:25,360
He's talkative. We're very close.

231
00:18:25,360 --> 00:18:27,920
He's the Fourth-in-Line.

232
00:18:27,920 --> 00:18:30,240
That one runs his mouth.

233
00:18:30,240 --> 00:18:34,320
<i>The third one has a keen interest in astronomy.</i>

234
00:18:34,880 --> 00:18:38,320
Is there any prince
who enjoys going out and about?

235
00:18:39,680 --> 00:18:41,480
That's Prince Fah Haam.

236
00:18:42,920 --> 00:18:46,680
He has no seat on the royal council
that governs the kingdom.

237
00:18:46,680 --> 00:18:48,160
<i>An artist.</i>

238
00:18:48,160 --> 00:18:49,440
[4th Prince: Artist]

239
00:18:49,440 --> 00:18:53,400
The youngest prince is Prince Jom Harn.

240
00:18:53,400 --> 00:18:55,520
He's the Fifth-in-Line.

241
00:18:56,400 --> 00:18:58,760
<i>The fifth prince is skilled in combat.</i>

242
00:18:58,760 --> 00:19:00,480
[5th Prince: Combat]

243
00:19:00,480 --> 00:19:02,920
Is that all?

244
00:19:02,920 --> 00:19:04,800
There's one more.

245
00:19:04,800 --> 00:19:08,600
Is he tall, with a stern face,
an intimidating look,

246
00:19:08,600 --> 00:19:11,000
and scars all over his body?

247
00:19:12,040 --> 00:19:14,280
You know my brother Mueang Fah?

248
00:19:15,400 --> 00:19:17,640
Prince Mueang Fah.

249
00:19:19,000 --> 00:19:22,400
He was sent to a city on the border as a child.

250
00:19:22,400 --> 00:19:26,680
How do you know he has scars all over his body?

251
00:19:30,120 --> 00:19:31,960
I...

252
00:19:31,960 --> 00:19:36,240
I've heard people talk about it.

253
00:19:36,240 --> 00:19:39,120
So there are six princes, correct?

254
00:19:40,720 --> 00:19:44,440
<i>Most of the princes have different mothers,</i>

255
00:19:44,440 --> 00:19:46,640
<i>but they've been close since childhood.</i>

256
00:19:46,640 --> 00:19:49,840
<i>Still, no matter how close they are,</i>

257
00:19:49,840 --> 00:19:54,920
<i>the fight for power can get brutal.</i>

258
00:19:56,160 --> 00:19:59,560
Prince Indraraja, Prince Saen Thep,

259
00:19:59,560 --> 00:20:05,040
Prince Kong Tai, Prince Fah Haam,
Prince Jom Harn, and Prince Mueang Fah.

260
00:20:05,040 --> 00:20:11,160
<i>Ullavee reached
its greatest prosperity under...</i>

261
00:20:11,160 --> 00:20:13,840
<i>Phaya Devaraja,</i>

262
00:20:13,840 --> 00:20:18,640
<i>its last and most ruthless king.</i>

263
00:20:19,360 --> 00:20:24,200
<i>He seized the throne
by murdering his own siblings.</i>

264
00:20:27,960 --> 00:20:30,680
Who's Phaya Devaraja?

265
00:20:38,920 --> 00:20:41,920
Seer Phrommaya has chosen an auspicious time
for the bedding ceremony.

266
00:20:41,920 --> 00:20:44,360
We only have a few days to prepare.

267
00:20:44,360 --> 00:20:46,680
After the Soul-Blessing Ceremony,

268
00:20:46,680 --> 00:20:50,720
your father and I will escort the two of you
to the bridal chamber.

269
00:20:50,720 --> 00:20:55,520
The ceremony must be grand and flawless,

270
00:20:55,520 --> 00:21:00,200
worthy of Saen Thep, a prince of Ullavee.

271
00:21:02,280 --> 00:21:04,240
Maneethip,

272
00:21:04,240 --> 00:21:06,520
I will have the maids from the powder room

273
00:21:06,520 --> 00:21:09,720
oil your hair, scrub your skin,

274
00:21:09,720 --> 00:21:12,240
steam your body, and apply a face mask.

275
00:21:12,240 --> 00:21:16,480
Everyone there should be in awe of you,

276
00:21:16,480 --> 00:21:24,040
and see that Saen Thep has chosen
a consort worthy of him.

277
00:21:28,040 --> 00:21:29,240
Yes.

278
00:21:31,000 --> 00:21:36,360
Tomorrow, the king will send
gold-thread silk and jewelry from Wiang Kaew

279
00:21:36,360 --> 00:21:38,680
for you to choose from.

280
00:21:39,440 --> 00:21:41,120
Yes.

281
00:21:41,120 --> 00:21:45,080
Everything must be done
with the dignity our station demands.

282
00:21:45,720 --> 00:21:48,960
Once Saen Thep becomes King,

283
00:21:49,520 --> 00:21:52,080
you shall be Queen.

284
00:21:52,080 --> 00:21:54,200
Let us get through this ceremony first, Mother.

285
00:21:54,200 --> 00:21:57,080
Her face turns pale
just talking about the preparations.

286
00:21:57,080 --> 00:21:59,440
Do not think of her as Queen just yet.

287
00:21:59,440 --> 00:22:01,840
Let her first learn to be a good consort.

288
00:22:01,840 --> 00:22:05,360
All I've heard her say is "Yes. Yes. Yes."

289
00:22:05,360 --> 00:22:07,840
Maneethip must be nervous

290
00:22:07,840 --> 00:22:10,360
about such an important ceremony.

291
00:22:10,360 --> 00:22:12,480
That's why she's been paying
such close attention.

292
00:22:14,320 --> 00:22:18,360
The truth is, you're happy about this too,

293
00:22:21,640 --> 00:22:23,200
are you not?

294
00:22:27,720 --> 00:22:28,920
Yes.

295
00:22:30,000 --> 00:22:31,720
Come with me.

296
00:22:31,720 --> 00:22:35,040
We will have the wardrobe maids
take your measurements

297
00:22:35,040 --> 00:22:37,840
so we can prepare the right tube skirt for you.

298
00:22:37,840 --> 00:22:39,080
Yes.

299
00:22:54,080 --> 00:22:56,480
Are you sure, Saen Thep,

300
00:22:56,480 --> 00:23:00,280
this is the woman
you fell in love with at first sight?

301
00:23:00,280 --> 00:23:02,880
The one you rushed home

302
00:23:02,880 --> 00:23:06,200
to ask Father to arrange a marriage with?

303
00:23:06,200 --> 00:23:08,520
Are you sure you've got the right woman?

304
00:23:37,680 --> 00:23:41,160
Lady Fongnuan, your skirt is flying up!

305
00:23:42,240 --> 00:23:43,520
- See?
- Lady Fongnuan!

306
00:23:43,520 --> 00:23:45,200
- It's not hard at all.
- Careful, my lady.

307
00:23:46,640 --> 00:23:49,240
- Watch me, Lha.
- Yesterday, I managed to do this five times.

308
00:23:49,240 --> 00:23:51,600
- Please be careful.
- Lady Fongnuan.

309
00:23:51,600 --> 00:23:54,080
- Your skirt is flying up.
- Look!

310
00:23:54,080 --> 00:23:56,480
Come on. I'm going to let the ball go.

311
00:23:56,480 --> 00:24:00,400
Ready, Lha? One, two, three! Here!

312
00:24:03,400 --> 00:24:05,040
I'm fine.

313
00:24:05,040 --> 00:24:09,320
I think we should stop.
If Princess Maneethip sees us, she'll scold us.

314
00:24:09,320 --> 00:24:11,680
I can play by myself. You sit and rest, Lha.

315
00:24:11,680 --> 00:24:13,480
- Lady Fongnuan!
- Fongnuan.

316
00:24:14,120 --> 00:24:15,400
Lha.

317
00:24:16,880 --> 00:24:18,520
Stop playing already.

318
00:24:18,520 --> 00:24:19,920
Come back inside.

319
00:24:20,960 --> 00:24:22,280
My lady.

320
00:24:30,040 --> 00:24:31,360
Please stop, my lady.

321
00:24:31,360 --> 00:24:33,160
Princess Maneethip has come
to fetch us back inside.

322
00:24:33,160 --> 00:24:35,240
Lha!

323
00:24:35,960 --> 00:24:37,680
It's time to go, my lady.

324
00:24:40,280 --> 00:24:43,480
- Lady Fongnuan!
- I know.

325
00:25:08,840 --> 00:25:10,320
I'm full.

326
00:25:15,480 --> 00:25:17,560
Are you so excited after discussing

327
00:25:17,560 --> 00:25:20,000
the bedding ceremony
that you've lost your appetite?

328
00:25:25,720 --> 00:25:27,760
Quite the opposite.

329
00:25:50,680 --> 00:25:51,840
Lha,

330
00:25:54,280 --> 00:25:57,080
why doesn't she seem excited?

331
00:25:57,080 --> 00:25:58,720
That's unusual.

332
00:25:59,400 --> 00:26:01,920
Do you not remember, Lady Fongnuan?

333
00:26:06,080 --> 00:26:08,560
I must have forgotten a few things.

334
00:26:09,680 --> 00:26:11,800
Could you tell me?

335
00:26:11,800 --> 00:26:14,720
I cannot speak of my masters' affairs.

336
00:26:16,040 --> 00:26:18,320
It is for the best that you do not remember.

337
00:26:19,840 --> 00:26:23,000
If you don't tell me, I'll ask her myself.

338
00:26:23,000 --> 00:26:24,560
Please don't, my lady.

339
00:26:26,800 --> 00:26:30,440
If you don't want Princess Maneethip
to suffer any more,

340
00:26:30,440 --> 00:26:32,560
please don't ask her.

341
00:26:32,560 --> 00:26:34,400
I beg you.

342
00:27:14,440 --> 00:27:17,520
Prince Saen Thep seems like a good man.

343
00:27:17,520 --> 00:27:22,880
He's kind, patient,
and he seems to love her dearly.

344
00:27:25,480 --> 00:27:27,920
If I were her,

345
00:27:27,920 --> 00:27:29,640
I'd be happy.

346
00:28:54,880 --> 00:28:56,640
If one day,

347
00:28:59,120 --> 00:29:01,960
I earn enough money to buy back your freedom,

348
00:29:02,920 --> 00:29:04,840
let us get out of here...

349
00:29:06,160 --> 00:29:08,920
and start a new life together, Nam Nang.

350
00:29:08,920 --> 00:29:11,000
My price is rather high.

351
00:29:12,360 --> 00:29:14,840
Where would a musician like you...

352
00:29:14,840 --> 00:29:17,440
find the money to buy my freedom?

353
00:29:26,600 --> 00:29:28,760
What if I could?

354
00:29:35,120 --> 00:29:39,880
Getting to the top here was no easy feat.

355
00:29:39,880 --> 00:29:44,920
You want me to leave everything and start over?

356
00:29:44,920 --> 00:29:46,400
Why?

357
00:29:53,360 --> 00:29:55,640
Because of my love.

358
00:30:02,920 --> 00:30:05,080
Love does not exist.

359
00:30:06,600 --> 00:30:09,080
There is only pleasure and desire,

360
00:30:09,760 --> 00:30:12,360
and the bonds that time and fate create.

361
00:30:16,480 --> 00:30:19,400
I will not risk my life.

362
00:30:19,400 --> 00:30:21,680
The outside world is frightening.

363
00:30:23,600 --> 00:30:28,320
No amount of love can withstand it.

364
00:30:31,880 --> 00:30:34,200
If you love me,

365
00:30:38,080 --> 00:30:40,560
then simply come and see me here.

366
00:30:52,120 --> 00:30:54,080
If I have to pay the tribute twice,

367
00:30:54,080 --> 00:30:57,320
how am I supposed to make a profit
from my business?

368
00:30:57,320 --> 00:31:01,760
This is Crown Prince Indraraja's order.
Do you dare defy it?

369
00:31:02,320 --> 00:31:07,160
If you have so many problems,
then pack up and go home.

370
00:31:08,240 --> 00:31:11,520
And do not expect to trade in Ullavee again.

371
00:31:12,320 --> 00:31:16,040
No, Your Highness.
I'm just surprised, that's all.

372
00:31:16,040 --> 00:31:20,000
I have never heard of such a rule in Ullavee.

373
00:31:21,240 --> 00:31:23,280
There are bandits
all along the border these days,

374
00:31:23,280 --> 00:31:26,120
waiting to rob passing caravans.

375
00:31:26,120 --> 00:31:29,640
Without protection tribute,

376
00:31:29,640 --> 00:31:33,720
Crown Prince Indraraja won't send soldiers
to guard your caravan.

377
00:31:35,480 --> 00:31:38,760
Are you sure you can fend for yourselves?

378
00:31:50,440 --> 00:31:57,520
Here is the tribute from our caravan.
We ask for Crown Prince Indraraja's protection.

379
00:31:59,080 --> 00:32:01,160
I assure you,

380
00:32:01,160 --> 00:32:05,240
your caravan will remain safe and sound.

381
00:32:16,160 --> 00:32:17,520
And...

382
00:32:19,000 --> 00:32:20,360
what of you?

383
00:32:44,960 --> 00:32:47,200
Listen, all of you.

384
00:32:47,200 --> 00:32:52,480
From now on, anyone wishing to trade in Ullavee

385
00:32:52,480 --> 00:32:56,480
must pay tribute to Crown Prince Indraraja.

386
00:32:56,480 --> 00:32:58,600
There will be no exceptions.

387
00:33:00,640 --> 00:33:02,600
The Crown Prince...

388
00:33:02,600 --> 00:33:05,320
is demanding tribute for protection?

389
00:33:05,320 --> 00:33:07,440
It is nothing unusual.

390
00:33:07,440 --> 00:33:10,000
I've seen it time and time again.

391
00:33:10,000 --> 00:33:12,560
Nobles bribe their way into positions of power.

392
00:33:13,160 --> 00:33:16,880
Merchants pay protection fees to trade.

393
00:33:16,880 --> 00:33:21,040
The powerful find plenty of ways
to profit from their positions.

394
00:33:21,040 --> 00:33:25,240
If they collect tribute and pocket it

395
00:33:25,240 --> 00:33:27,840
instead of handing it over
to the Royal Treasury,

396
00:33:27,840 --> 00:33:30,000
that's a crime.

397
00:33:30,000 --> 00:33:32,320
That is the outside world for you.

398
00:33:33,720 --> 00:33:38,560
The powerful extort money from ordinary people
without fear of the law.

399
00:33:38,560 --> 00:33:41,160
Even caravan merchants
face this much oppression.

400
00:33:41,160 --> 00:33:45,160
Imagine how much worse off I'd be.

401
00:33:49,600 --> 00:33:52,440
Not all nobles are like that.

402
00:33:55,080 --> 00:33:58,000
You speak as if you're one of them.

403
00:35:09,200 --> 00:35:12,600
My sister asked me to return the unused fabric.

404
00:35:14,680 --> 00:35:16,560
Come, sit up here.

405
00:35:22,600 --> 00:35:24,840
Have you chosen yours?

406
00:35:26,160 --> 00:35:29,840
The king picked these out
for you and my sister.

407
00:35:29,840 --> 00:35:33,680
I couldn't possibly wear them.
I don't want to get too big for my boots.

408
00:35:34,240 --> 00:35:36,160
Too big for your boots?

409
00:35:38,600 --> 00:35:46,000
- What does that have to do with anything?
- I'm talking nonsense again, aren't I?

410
00:35:46,000 --> 00:35:47,440
It's all right.

411
00:35:47,440 --> 00:35:50,760
Go ahead and say it.
It's actually quite funny.

412
00:35:50,760 --> 00:35:55,080
It's better than before,
when you wouldn't say a word.

413
00:35:55,080 --> 00:35:58,720
I was mute before, so now I'm mad instead.

414
00:36:14,240 --> 00:36:16,000
Was I smiling too much?

415
00:36:17,080 --> 00:36:19,160
Is that why you're making that face?

416
00:36:19,160 --> 00:36:21,400
It's nice to see you smile.

417
00:36:21,400 --> 00:36:24,160
Much better than when you give me a stern look.

418
00:36:25,480 --> 00:36:31,280
If you hadn't made me worry at the ceremony,

419
00:36:31,280 --> 00:36:32,720
I wouldn't have scolded you.

420
00:36:35,920 --> 00:36:37,400
Let me pick one for you.

421
00:37:00,680 --> 00:37:02,640
This one suits you.

422
00:37:04,960 --> 00:37:06,800
It looks vibrant.

423
00:37:08,280 --> 00:37:09,680
It's yours.

424
00:37:10,680 --> 00:37:12,360
Thank you.

425
00:37:33,080 --> 00:37:35,320
You and your sister are...

426
00:37:36,600 --> 00:37:37,760
strange.

427
00:37:40,160 --> 00:37:42,560
The first time I met Maneethip,

428
00:37:43,520 --> 00:37:47,640
she was cheerful and full of life.

429
00:37:49,840 --> 00:37:51,440
But you were quiet.

430
00:37:52,080 --> 00:37:54,080
You wouldn't say a word.

431
00:37:54,080 --> 00:37:56,560
You looked weary and listless.

432
00:37:58,240 --> 00:37:59,760
But now,

433
00:38:00,560 --> 00:38:02,320
it's like you and Maneethip...

434
00:38:03,200 --> 00:38:05,360
switched bodies.

435
00:38:06,920 --> 00:38:09,000
Maneethip has grown quiet,

436
00:38:09,880 --> 00:38:15,320
while you... never fail to make me smile.

437
00:38:20,480 --> 00:38:21,880
Fongnuan.

438
00:38:22,880 --> 00:38:24,440
Fongnuan.

439
00:38:26,240 --> 00:38:27,520
Yes?

440
00:38:29,080 --> 00:38:31,080
I have to head to the Royal Library.

441
00:38:31,080 --> 00:38:33,800
I have a meeting with Seer Phrommaya.

442
00:38:33,800 --> 00:38:36,000
Please take that piece of fabric

443
00:38:36,000 --> 00:38:38,560
and tell Maneethip I wanted you to have it.

444
00:38:38,560 --> 00:38:41,120
I look forward to seeing you wear it
on the day of the ceremony.

445
00:38:43,080 --> 00:38:44,640
Thank you.

446
00:39:28,080 --> 00:39:30,520
You can't feel like this, Boon.

447
00:39:33,040 --> 00:39:35,160
You're Fongnuan now.

448
00:39:58,080 --> 00:39:59,800
A birthday celebration?

449
00:40:00,520 --> 00:40:01,840
Yes.

450
00:40:02,520 --> 00:40:05,760
I have much to attend to before my ceremony.

451
00:40:05,760 --> 00:40:09,640
I'd like you to prepare a gift
for Prince Kong Tai on my behalf.

452
00:40:11,000 --> 00:40:14,400
What kind of gifts
do people give each other here?

453
00:40:14,400 --> 00:40:18,080
Prince Saen Thep said
Prince Kong Tai is having bad luck.

454
00:40:18,080 --> 00:40:21,440
I think a Hawk's Eye Amulet may be a good idea.

455
00:40:22,280 --> 00:40:23,800
A Hawk's Eye Amulet?

456
00:40:24,400 --> 00:40:26,280
What is that?

457
00:40:27,000 --> 00:40:30,240
It's an amulet to ward off evil.

458
00:40:30,240 --> 00:40:32,680
It's made from bamboo strips

459
00:40:32,680 --> 00:40:34,560
woven into the shape of a hawk's eye.

460
00:40:36,320 --> 00:40:40,640
That sounds like a good idea.
Where can we buy a Hawk's Eye Amulet?

461
00:40:40,640 --> 00:40:42,520
There's no need to buy it.

462
00:40:42,520 --> 00:40:45,840
You can make one yourself. It's very easy.

463
00:40:48,200 --> 00:40:51,040
The scrubbing is done.
Now, let us rinse you off.

464
00:40:51,800 --> 00:40:53,360
Lha,

465
00:40:53,360 --> 00:40:56,000
please help Fongnuan make a Hawk's Eye Amulet.

466
00:40:56,000 --> 00:40:57,120
Yes, my lady.

467
00:40:57,120 --> 00:41:01,320
Fongnuan, do not be too mischievous
and do not make me worry.

468
00:41:01,320 --> 00:41:04,280
- Do you understand?
- Yes, sister.

469
00:41:05,080 --> 00:41:07,680
Go on, and be back soon.

470
00:41:07,680 --> 00:41:09,320
Before nightfall.

471
00:41:09,320 --> 00:41:10,480
Very well.

472
00:41:16,800 --> 00:41:21,080
Lha, is a Hawk's Eye Amulet
really easy to make?

473
00:41:26,360 --> 00:41:28,880
You call this easy?

474
00:41:29,760 --> 00:41:32,520
It's not difficult at all, my lady.
Please give it a try.

475
00:41:32,520 --> 00:41:37,200
Choose straight bamboo
so we can get straight strips.

476
00:41:39,040 --> 00:41:41,280
Will this one do?

477
00:41:41,280 --> 00:41:45,240
Lady Fongnuan, aim, then chop.

478
00:41:45,240 --> 00:41:47,840
Aim, then chop?

479
00:41:47,840 --> 00:41:49,000
Yes.

480
00:41:53,280 --> 00:41:55,520
Could you use a little more force?

481
00:41:57,280 --> 00:42:00,720
A little more force, please. A little more.

482
00:42:11,120 --> 00:42:14,880
I think we should go cut down
that clump of bamboo over there.

483
00:42:14,880 --> 00:42:17,280
They're all straight stalks.

484
00:42:17,280 --> 00:42:21,120
Leave this here for now.

485
00:42:21,120 --> 00:42:23,040
Let us go.

486
00:42:23,040 --> 00:42:24,600
- Lha!
- Please follow me.

487
00:42:24,600 --> 00:42:27,440
Lha, wait! Lha, wait!

488
00:42:27,440 --> 00:42:29,080
This way!

489
00:42:32,760 --> 00:42:34,400
Lha, wait for me!

490
00:42:36,360 --> 00:42:38,760
Lha! Wait for me!

491
00:42:40,200 --> 00:42:42,560
Lady Fongnuan, follow me quickly!

492
00:42:43,400 --> 00:42:45,280
Wait for me!

493
00:42:47,680 --> 00:42:49,440
Lha!

494
00:42:53,480 --> 00:42:55,920
This way, Lady Fongnuan! This way!

495
00:42:58,560 --> 00:43:00,160
Right this way!

496
00:43:01,200 --> 00:43:02,480
Lha!

497
00:43:02,480 --> 00:43:03,560
I found it, Lady Fongnuan!

498
00:43:03,560 --> 00:43:05,480
- This way!
- Lha, wait!

499
00:43:05,480 --> 00:43:07,640
- There it is!
- Lha!

500
00:43:07,640 --> 00:43:09,520
Lha, wait!

501
00:43:09,520 --> 00:43:11,000
Lady Fongnuan!

502
00:43:12,600 --> 00:43:13,720
Lady Fongnuan?

503
00:43:13,720 --> 00:43:17,800
Lha, I'm here.

504
00:43:17,800 --> 00:43:19,400
Lady Fongnuan!

505
00:43:21,720 --> 00:43:23,760
Lady Fongnuan! Are you hurt?

506
00:43:23,760 --> 00:43:26,560
This way. Can you get up, my lady?

507
00:43:27,320 --> 00:43:28,960
Careful.

508
00:43:32,120 --> 00:43:34,720
Lady Fongnuan! Are you hurt anywhere?

509
00:43:36,320 --> 00:43:38,720
You didn't wait for me.

510
00:43:38,720 --> 00:43:41,240
I'm sorry, my lady.

511
00:43:41,240 --> 00:43:43,120
You're not hurt, are you?

512
00:43:49,320 --> 00:43:52,840
We're lucky this animal trap is old.

513
00:43:53,720 --> 00:43:58,720
Otherwise, those sharpened bamboo stakes
could've impaled you.

514
00:44:01,880 --> 00:44:04,040
I almost died.

515
00:44:04,040 --> 00:44:07,960
Let me cut the bamboo myself.

516
00:44:07,960 --> 00:44:10,320
Please wait for me here, my lady.

517
00:44:14,200 --> 00:44:16,520
Stay here. Don't go anywhere.

518
00:44:16,520 --> 00:44:17,880
I'll stay right here.

519
00:44:20,120 --> 00:44:21,640
Come back soon.

520
00:44:21,640 --> 00:44:22,880
Yes, my lady.

521
00:44:36,440 --> 00:44:38,160
Hey! That way!

522
00:44:40,000 --> 00:44:41,880
Hey! Stop!

523
00:44:53,360 --> 00:44:54,760
Stop right there!

524
00:44:58,880 --> 00:45:01,800
There! After him! Come on!

525
00:45:01,800 --> 00:45:04,320
- Stop right there!
- Stop!

526
00:45:07,600 --> 00:45:11,960
- Hey! Stop!
- Hey, stop right there! Hey!

527
00:45:12,560 --> 00:45:15,280
- He's going that way!
- Stop right there!

528
00:45:18,920 --> 00:45:21,840
Your Highness! Your Highness!

529
00:45:21,840 --> 00:45:23,200
Come here!

530
00:45:36,760 --> 00:45:37,920
Down!

531
00:45:37,920 --> 00:45:40,120
- Stop!
- Stop right there!

532
00:45:42,640 --> 00:45:44,480
Hey! Stop!

533
00:45:44,480 --> 00:45:47,240
- Stop right there!
- Hey! Stop!

534
00:45:48,480 --> 00:45:50,120
Where did he go?

535
00:45:50,120 --> 00:45:51,360
Hey, you.

536
00:45:52,040 --> 00:45:56,080
- Did you see a young man come this way?
- You mean the shirtless one?

537
00:45:56,080 --> 00:46:01,720
He went that way. He was running so fast.
He must be long gone by now. Hurry after him.

538
00:46:01,720 --> 00:46:04,360
- Let's go! Hurry after him!
- Move!

539
00:46:10,280 --> 00:46:11,920
You trust people too easily.

540
00:46:12,960 --> 00:46:14,080
Your Highness!

541
00:46:16,240 --> 00:46:18,560
Your Highness! You're safe now.

542
00:46:20,960 --> 00:46:22,120
They're gone.

543
00:46:39,240 --> 00:46:40,640
Thanks.

544
00:46:44,400 --> 00:46:46,200
You're the madwoman.

545
00:46:46,800 --> 00:46:49,160
I'm not.

546
00:46:49,160 --> 00:46:51,080
I'm tired of explaining.

547
00:46:52,840 --> 00:46:55,960
What did you do, anyway?

548
00:46:55,960 --> 00:46:58,000
Why were they chasing you?

549
00:47:02,560 --> 00:47:06,040
<i>Whoever ends up with the most marks... loses.</i>

550
00:47:17,480 --> 00:47:21,840
You knew they were drugging their opponents.

551
00:47:21,840 --> 00:47:23,680
So why get involved?

552
00:47:32,960 --> 00:47:37,080
<i>- Come on! Go!
- Come on!</i>

553
00:47:37,080 --> 00:47:38,840
<i>- Go!
- Go!</i>

554
00:47:38,840 --> 00:47:40,720
<i>- Fight!
- Fight!</i>

555
00:47:40,720 --> 00:47:42,560
<i>- Get him!
- Come on!</i>

556
00:47:42,560 --> 00:47:44,800
<i>- Get him!
- Get in there!</i>

557
00:47:44,800 --> 00:47:46,040
<i>- Get him!
- Get him!</i>

558
00:47:46,040 --> 00:47:49,120
<i>- Hurry up!
- Get him!</i>

559
00:47:51,880 --> 00:47:54,200
<i>Get up!</i>

560
00:47:54,200 --> 00:47:55,640
<i>Fight!</i>

561
00:47:59,880 --> 00:48:01,360
<i>Hit him!</i>

562
00:48:03,520 --> 00:48:06,480
<i>- Get up!
- Get up!</i>

563
00:48:06,480 --> 00:48:07,960
<i>Watch out!</i>

564
00:48:09,000 --> 00:48:10,680
<i>- Fight! Fight!
- Fight! Fight!</i>

565
00:48:11,400 --> 00:48:13,080
<i>- Fight!
- Fight!</i>

566
00:48:13,080 --> 00:48:15,360
<i>- Fight!
- Fight!</i>

567
00:48:23,080 --> 00:48:25,080
<i>- Fight!
- Fight!</i>

568
00:48:25,080 --> 00:48:27,200
<i>Fight!</i>

569
00:48:27,200 --> 00:48:30,320
<i>Fight! Fight! Fight!</i>

570
00:48:30,320 --> 00:48:32,680
<i>Come on! Get up!</i>

571
00:48:32,680 --> 00:48:36,480
<i>Hey! Come on! Nice!</i>

572
00:48:36,480 --> 00:48:39,880
<i>Go! Come on!</i>

573
00:48:42,040 --> 00:48:43,360
<i>Keep going!</i>

574
00:48:44,160 --> 00:48:45,560
<i>He's losing!</i>

575
00:48:52,080 --> 00:48:53,760
<i>- Go!
- Go!</i>

576
00:48:55,560 --> 00:48:57,320
<i>- Get up!
- Keep going!</i>

577
00:49:05,000 --> 00:49:06,800
<i>Damn it!</i>

578
00:49:08,000 --> 00:49:09,720
<i>You cheated!</i>

579
00:49:09,720 --> 00:49:12,120
<i>Hey! How could you possibly lose?</i>

580
00:49:12,120 --> 00:49:14,760
<i>- I made him drink the water.
- I saw him drink it with my own eyes.</i>

581
00:49:14,760 --> 00:49:17,040
<i>Damn it! How could you lose?</i>

582
00:49:19,880 --> 00:49:21,480
<i>Hey!</i>

583
00:49:21,480 --> 00:49:23,520
<i>Where do you think you're going? Stop!</i>

584
00:49:23,520 --> 00:49:26,040
<i>- Hey, stop!
- Hey!</i>

585
00:49:26,040 --> 00:49:27,040
<i>Stop!</i>

586
00:49:27,040 --> 00:49:30,280
<i>Come on! Come on, winners!</i>

587
00:49:31,080 --> 00:49:32,920
<i>Tough luck, losers!</i>

588
00:49:35,000 --> 00:49:38,720
If you hadn't run into me,
they would've beaten you up.

589
00:49:38,720 --> 00:49:40,400
Then what would you have done?

590
00:49:44,200 --> 00:49:47,560
You're... quite clever.

591
00:49:47,560 --> 00:49:51,280
You saved me without anyone getting hurt.

592
00:49:52,280 --> 00:49:55,760
I'm in your debt this time.

593
00:49:55,760 --> 00:49:57,440
Tell me how I can repay you.

594
00:49:57,440 --> 00:50:01,440
No need. It's nothing.

595
00:50:01,440 --> 00:50:05,240
Just stop calling me a madwoman. That's all.

596
00:50:13,120 --> 00:50:15,600
Your face looks younger than mine.

597
00:50:15,600 --> 00:50:17,720
So I'll call you...

598
00:50:20,360 --> 00:50:21,920
junior.

599
00:50:24,200 --> 00:50:27,480
And you shall call me...

600
00:50:27,480 --> 00:50:28,840
senior.

601
00:50:30,160 --> 00:50:31,960
All right.

602
00:50:31,960 --> 00:50:33,360
Deal.

603
00:50:36,040 --> 00:50:37,640
Deal?

604
00:50:37,640 --> 00:50:40,480
"Deal," like this. Not like that.

605
00:50:41,800 --> 00:50:43,680
Deal.

606
00:50:44,440 --> 00:50:46,480
- Deal.
- Deal.

607
00:50:48,560 --> 00:50:49,640
Here.

608
00:50:50,600 --> 00:50:54,000
It means we're agreed.

609
00:50:54,000 --> 00:50:55,080
- Deal.
- Deal.

610
00:50:55,080 --> 00:50:56,800
- Deal.
- Deal.

611
00:50:56,800 --> 00:50:59,120
- Deal.
- Deal.

612
00:50:59,120 --> 00:51:00,720
- Deal.
- Deal.

613
00:51:00,720 --> 00:51:01,800
Deal.

614
00:51:02,520 --> 00:51:03,440
That's enough.

615
00:51:03,440 --> 00:51:05,280
- Deal.
- That's enough.

616
00:51:20,280 --> 00:51:23,280
You should hurry along
before those men return.

617
00:51:25,200 --> 00:51:28,280
I... shall take my leave then,

618
00:51:28,880 --> 00:51:30,120
junior.

619
00:51:36,040 --> 00:51:37,640
I'm back.

620
00:51:38,480 --> 00:51:40,040
I'm back, my lady.

621
00:51:41,760 --> 00:51:45,480
Lha! Do we really have to carry this much back?

622
00:51:45,480 --> 00:51:47,240
This is not all.

623
00:51:56,440 --> 00:51:59,080
- Where does she get all that energy?
- Lady Fongnuan! Watch out!

624
00:52:00,200 --> 00:52:01,720
Lha!

625
00:52:04,920 --> 00:52:07,600
- That's enough.
- That's not all.

626
00:52:07,600 --> 00:52:10,960
Lha! I can't carry all this.

627
00:52:22,760 --> 00:52:24,320
How infuriating.

628
00:52:33,360 --> 00:52:34,400
- Get up!
- Get up!

629
00:52:34,400 --> 00:52:36,160
- Hey! Hey!
- Get up!

630
00:52:36,160 --> 00:52:39,640
- Let go!
- Let go of me! Let go of me!

631
00:52:39,640 --> 00:52:42,680
Hey! Let go!

632
00:52:42,680 --> 00:52:44,080
Let go of me!

633
00:52:52,320 --> 00:52:53,880
- Let go!
- Bring them in.

634
00:52:53,880 --> 00:52:55,200
Let go of me!

635
00:52:55,200 --> 00:52:58,000
- Let go!
- Sit down!

636
00:52:58,000 --> 00:52:59,560
These are the men

637
00:52:59,560 --> 00:53:02,600
who ambushed our caravan
and stole our livestock.

638
00:53:02,600 --> 00:53:04,920
How dare you steal what is mine?

639
00:53:05,760 --> 00:53:07,440
Aren't you afraid to die?

640
00:53:12,440 --> 00:53:14,040
Those are mine.

641
00:53:14,040 --> 00:53:17,640
You and Prince Indraraja stole them from me!

642
00:53:18,840 --> 00:53:22,120
Trade has been so difficult
that I have nothing left.

643
00:53:23,640 --> 00:53:26,080
I'd rather fight to the death than starve!

644
00:53:28,200 --> 00:53:31,600
The whole of Ullavee and Merng Mang will hear

645
00:53:31,600 --> 00:53:36,280
that Crown Princes like you two are deceitful

646
00:53:36,280 --> 00:53:37,840
and exploit us common folk!

647
00:53:55,520 --> 00:53:57,520
People like you...

648
00:53:58,200 --> 00:54:00,560
have no right to negotiate with me.

649
00:54:01,400 --> 00:54:02,800
Low-born churl.

650
00:55:17,120 --> 00:55:19,840
When I went to the Courtesan House,

651
00:55:19,840 --> 00:55:23,920
I saw Pha Wiang use Indraraja's name

652
00:55:24,600 --> 00:55:29,960
to extort protection money
from Siao caravan merchants.

653
00:55:33,440 --> 00:55:35,160
Then suddenly,

654
00:55:35,160 --> 00:55:39,520
the merchants were dragged away.

655
00:55:39,520 --> 00:55:42,600
I had a bad feeling, so I followed them.

656
00:55:42,600 --> 00:55:44,520
When I found them again,
they were already dead.

657
00:55:47,400 --> 00:55:49,680
This is a grave matter, Mueang Fah.

658
00:55:52,960 --> 00:55:56,240
Why are you telling me this?

659
00:55:56,240 --> 00:55:59,200
I believe you love Ullavee

660
00:55:59,800 --> 00:56:04,280
and won't let someone like
Prince Pha Wiang from Merng Mang

661
00:56:04,280 --> 00:56:06,200
profit off our kingdom.

662
00:56:11,840 --> 00:56:13,680
Why do you believe so?

663
00:56:14,440 --> 00:56:15,960
My heart tells me so.

664
00:56:17,560 --> 00:56:20,760
I haven't told anyone else about this but you.

665
00:56:21,960 --> 00:56:25,560
What you do next is up to you.

666
00:56:25,560 --> 00:56:27,800
This matter requires careful thought.

667
00:56:34,040 --> 00:56:35,640
By the way,

668
00:56:38,320 --> 00:56:40,760
what were you doing at the Courtesan House?

669
00:56:42,480 --> 00:56:45,720
A prince sneaking off
to the Courtesan House is wrong.

670
00:56:46,560 --> 00:56:49,040
It's a serious violation
of the Royal Residence's rules.

671
00:56:49,040 --> 00:56:53,000
If someone sees you
and word gets back to the king,

672
00:56:53,000 --> 00:56:54,920
you will be severely punished.

673
00:56:55,640 --> 00:56:58,320
I just happened to be passing by.

674
00:56:58,320 --> 00:56:59,600
You're lying.

675
00:57:07,120 --> 00:57:09,560
What I did is of no consequence.

676
00:57:10,880 --> 00:57:14,360
At least I got valuable information
for the kingdom.

677
00:57:17,560 --> 00:57:21,880
I couldn't have caught the thieves
without entering their den.

678
00:57:25,480 --> 00:57:29,120
I ask that you keep this a secret

679
00:57:29,720 --> 00:57:34,240
until we know for certain
whether Indraraja is involved.

680
00:57:39,160 --> 00:57:41,240
You may go.

681
00:57:41,240 --> 00:57:43,480
I'll take care of the bodies.

682
00:59:24,960 --> 00:59:27,640
Someone saw Pha Wiang using your name

683
00:59:28,280 --> 00:59:31,480
to collect protection tribute
from the caravan merchants.

684
00:59:32,560 --> 00:59:34,720
He threatened that if they didn't pay,

685
00:59:35,440 --> 00:59:38,680
you wouldn't send soldiers to protect them

686
00:59:38,680 --> 00:59:40,720
from the bandits at the border.

687
00:59:46,200 --> 00:59:48,000
Who told you this?

688
00:59:52,320 --> 00:59:53,720
A well-wisher.

689
00:59:58,320 --> 01:00:00,040
Do you believe them?

690
01:00:04,280 --> 01:00:07,760
I don't care if it's true or not.

691
01:00:10,960 --> 01:00:15,480
A little extorted money from the common folk?

692
01:00:15,480 --> 01:00:17,280
I have no desire for that.

693
01:00:18,000 --> 01:00:20,320
I don't believe Pha Wiang did it.

694
01:00:21,040 --> 01:00:24,600
What you've heard is false.

695
01:00:27,360 --> 01:00:31,080
But there were witnesses,
and some people died.

696
01:00:32,480 --> 01:00:35,640
Collecting tribute is one thing.

697
01:00:36,640 --> 01:00:39,520
But merchants from Siao have died.

698
01:00:40,240 --> 01:00:42,560
If this escalates

699
01:00:42,560 --> 01:00:45,880
and affects relations between our cities,

700
01:00:45,880 --> 01:00:47,880
it will become a serious matter.

701
01:00:52,200 --> 01:00:55,280
I'd like you to see
this matter properly resolved.

702
01:00:58,920 --> 01:01:01,640
In the future, you will rule Ullavee.

703
01:01:03,280 --> 01:01:05,360
If this is true,

704
01:01:06,040 --> 01:01:08,360
it's not worth risking your throne.

705
01:01:09,760 --> 01:01:14,640
But if you have no part in this,
you would do well to be cautious,

706
01:01:15,200 --> 01:01:19,800
for what Pha Wiang did is serious.

707
01:01:25,960 --> 01:01:30,320
This time, I'll risk my life to hide the truth.

708
01:01:31,760 --> 01:01:34,240
But let this be the last time.

709
01:01:44,320 --> 01:01:46,520
I will see to this myself.

710
01:01:46,520 --> 01:01:48,280
If it is true,

711
01:01:49,120 --> 01:01:52,320
I will not let it tarnish my honor.

712
01:02:20,400 --> 01:02:24,360
All of this is for you.

713
01:02:25,240 --> 01:02:26,920
You've done very well.

714
01:02:39,680 --> 01:02:45,240
All this money and these valuables
will secure your Crown Prince title.

715
01:02:45,240 --> 01:02:47,160
It will never be shaken.

716
01:02:48,040 --> 01:02:51,920
Whatever it takes to help you
take the Ullavee throne,

717
01:02:51,920 --> 01:02:53,960
I'm willing to do it.

718
01:02:54,680 --> 01:02:56,160
Thank you, brother.

719
01:02:57,400 --> 01:02:59,920
But be careful next time.

720
01:03:00,520 --> 01:03:02,960
Someone's watching us.

721
01:03:04,080 --> 01:03:05,600
Is it Mueang Fah?

722
01:03:06,720 --> 01:03:08,040
It's someone else.

723
01:03:10,440 --> 01:03:13,040
But Mueang Fah came to warn me

724
01:03:13,680 --> 01:03:18,200
that someone saw you
using my name to demand tribute.

725
01:03:18,200 --> 01:03:21,840
They also saw you kill the Siao merchants
to silence them.

726
01:03:23,800 --> 01:03:28,760
- Is it true?
- Did he tell you... who informed him?

727
01:03:29,800 --> 01:03:32,560
Someone like Mueang Fah
would never let it slip.

728
01:03:34,880 --> 01:03:36,520
That damn Mueang Fah.

729
01:03:37,640 --> 01:03:39,440
He keeps finding ways
to cause me trouble at every turn.

730
01:03:39,440 --> 01:03:42,800
If you hadn't shown him a weakness to exploit,

731
01:03:42,800 --> 01:03:45,040
you wouldn't have to be angry now.

732
01:03:48,600 --> 01:03:50,240
My apologies, brother.

733
01:03:50,240 --> 01:03:53,560
I'll be more careful from now on.

734
01:03:54,240 --> 01:03:56,440
Make sure no one learns of this.

735
01:03:57,600 --> 01:04:00,680
Or we'll die like those merchants.

736
01:04:02,120 --> 01:04:04,440
If Mueang Fah doesn't speak,

737
01:04:04,440 --> 01:04:06,360
no one will know.

738
01:04:07,320 --> 01:04:09,320
But who knows...

739
01:04:10,360 --> 01:04:12,280
how trustworthy he really is?

740
01:04:14,160 --> 01:04:18,200
Honestly, I can't stand him.

741
01:04:18,200 --> 01:04:20,960
He doesn't seem to be of much help to us.

742
01:04:20,960 --> 01:04:23,480
Now that he knows our secret,

743
01:04:23,480 --> 01:04:24,880
we can trust him even less.

744
01:04:24,880 --> 01:04:27,160
Since we can't fully trust him,

745
01:04:27,160 --> 01:04:29,440
we need to keep him close.

746
01:04:30,440 --> 01:04:33,600
I know Mueang Fah's weakness better
than anyone.

747
01:04:36,240 --> 01:04:38,960
He's still useful to us.

748
01:04:39,560 --> 01:04:42,160
Let's not let a trivial matter
ruin our big plan.

749
01:04:44,600 --> 01:04:47,120
I assured him it wasn't true.

750
01:04:47,120 --> 01:04:49,560
Stay calm and don't admit a thing.

751
01:04:49,560 --> 01:04:51,320
It will die down soon enough.

752
01:04:52,920 --> 01:04:57,360
Soon, we will both be kings.

753
01:04:58,280 --> 01:05:00,720
Ullavee and Wiang Merng Mang

754
01:05:00,720 --> 01:05:02,920
will rise together.

755
01:05:31,440 --> 01:05:35,360
I've prepared everything needed
for the ceremony.

756
01:05:35,360 --> 01:05:37,600
The venue is beautiful.

757
01:05:37,600 --> 01:05:40,640
There's nothing to worry about
with the Soul-Blessing Ceremony.

758
01:05:41,440 --> 01:05:44,400
Thank you ever so much, seer.

759
01:05:44,400 --> 01:05:46,320
You're most welcome, Your Highness.

760
01:05:49,320 --> 01:05:50,640
Wait.

761
01:05:59,400 --> 01:06:01,640
I bow before you, Royal Consort Chiang La-or.

762
01:06:03,000 --> 01:06:04,920
I have a question.

763
01:06:04,920 --> 01:06:09,000
Why is Mueang Fah still here?
Why hasn't he left for the border?

764
01:06:09,000 --> 01:06:14,840
Won't his staying here
bring bad luck to Ullavee?

765
01:06:16,080 --> 01:06:18,480
Don't think about that just yet, Mother.

766
01:06:19,120 --> 01:06:22,120
Let's focus on my bedding ceremony.

767
01:06:22,120 --> 01:06:27,120
I don't want someone else to ruin our ceremony.

768
01:06:29,520 --> 01:06:32,520
But if you have no objection,

769
01:06:32,520 --> 01:06:35,280
I won't press it.

770
01:06:35,280 --> 01:06:40,920
Either way, I truly appreciate
you taking care of everything.

771
01:06:42,960 --> 01:06:44,120
Of course.

772
01:07:22,600 --> 01:07:24,640
Look.

773
01:07:29,680 --> 01:07:33,160
Lady Fongnuan, that's impressive.

774
01:07:33,160 --> 01:07:36,600
You use different-colored threads.

775
01:07:36,600 --> 01:07:40,600
You've made these Hawk's Eye Amulets
unusually beautiful.

776
01:07:41,280 --> 01:07:42,520
Isn't this chic?

777
01:07:43,240 --> 01:07:44,360
Chic?

778
01:07:45,520 --> 01:07:46,760
Chic?

779
01:07:46,760 --> 01:07:49,800
Do you think you can do the same?

780
01:07:49,800 --> 01:07:51,360
Yes, my lady.

781
01:07:52,200 --> 01:07:57,360
Could you take over from here?
I'll hang this in the ceremony pavilion

782
01:07:57,360 --> 01:07:59,280
so we can see how many we'll need.

783
01:07:59,280 --> 01:08:00,440
Of course.

784
01:08:25,720 --> 01:08:27,440
<i>You've been through a lot.</i>

785
01:08:28,640 --> 01:08:30,280
<i>Are you talking to me?</i>

786
01:08:33,400 --> 01:08:35,680
<i>You lost your parents</i>

787
01:08:35,680 --> 01:08:37,680
<i>and the people you loved.</i>

788
01:08:37,680 --> 01:08:39,560
<i>Your boyfriend sucks.</i>

789
01:08:39,560 --> 01:08:41,280
<i>Your friend betrayed you.</i>

790
01:08:52,440 --> 01:08:53,720
<i>Am I right?</i>

791
01:08:54,840 --> 01:08:56,560
<i>Then that's how it is.</i>

792
01:08:57,400 --> 01:08:59,040
<i>You're right.</i>

793
01:08:59,040 --> 01:09:00,840
<i>How did you know?</i>

794
01:09:00,840 --> 01:09:03,040
<i>Are you a fortune teller?</i>

795
01:09:05,400 --> 01:09:08,040
<i>Some things are part of us.</i>

796
01:09:08,600 --> 01:09:12,440
<i>Our lives are more than what we see.</i>

797
01:09:13,880 --> 01:09:16,120
<i>There are also things...</i>

798
01:09:16,920 --> 01:09:18,400
<i>we cannot see.</i>

799
01:09:29,800 --> 01:09:31,640
<i>If you wish for something,</i>

800
01:09:31,640 --> 01:09:36,200
<i>Take this cone inside
and make a wish at the ancestral shrine.</i>

801
01:09:51,000 --> 01:09:52,880
That's the fortune-teller uncle.

802
01:10:01,240 --> 01:10:02,800
Fortune teller!

803
01:10:05,880 --> 01:10:07,080
Uncle!

804
01:10:10,240 --> 01:10:11,760
Where did he go?

805
01:10:59,680 --> 01:11:00,480
<i>I'll see you</i>
[Next Episode]

806
01:11:00,480 --> 01:11:01,920
<i>at Prince Kong Tai's birthday celebration.</i>

807
01:11:01,920 --> 01:11:03,600
<i>Enjoy yourself.</i>

808
01:11:03,600 --> 01:11:05,320
<i>I've taken care of everything.</i>

809
01:11:05,320 --> 01:11:06,640
<i>Cheers!</i>

810
01:11:06,640 --> 01:11:08,200
<i>Move!</i>

811
01:11:08,200 --> 01:11:09,480
<i>Do you wish to die?</i>

812
01:11:09,480 --> 01:11:12,600
<i>My lady, you look beautiful.</i>

813
01:11:12,600 --> 01:11:13,800
<i>Prince Mueang Fah.</i>

814
01:11:13,800 --> 01:11:17,080
<i>Thanks to you, I no longer wish to die.</i>

815
01:11:17,080 --> 01:11:19,560
<i>May your love grow ever stronger
and last forever.</i>

816
01:11:19,560 --> 01:11:22,160
<i>May you be blessed
with many children and grandchildren.</i>

817
01:11:22,160 --> 01:11:23,560
<i>Please take care of my sister.</i>

818
01:11:23,560 --> 01:11:24,880
<i>Please get out of my life.</i>

819
01:11:24,880 --> 01:11:26,040
<i>We shouldn't see each other again.</i>

820
01:11:26,040 --> 01:11:27,640
<i>Do you not love me anymore?</i>

821
01:11:27,640 --> 01:11:29,240
<i>What a modest celebration.</i>

822
01:11:29,240 --> 01:11:32,680
<i>Quite fitting for a consort
from a little place like Wang Nam Lin.</i>

823
01:11:32,680 --> 01:11:36,080
<i>Once I'm king,
I can give anyone whatever they want.</i>

824
01:11:36,080 --> 01:11:37,760
<i>Or do you disagree?</i>

825
01:11:39,480 --> 01:11:41,280
<i>Bew!</i>

826
01:11:41,280 --> 01:11:42,760
<i>Do you know him?</i>
